   "recap": "Episode 4, That's the Magic of Survivor, began the morning after Patt Cannaday was blindsided out of Toka. Danny Kilby asked who had voted for him, and four of his tribemates owned it. Brady Booker was furious at Carter Krull and Lewis Kelly. Jelly Loblack was sorry Patt was gone, and kept close the fact that Patt was the only person who knew about her hidden idol.\n\nTree Mail sent both tribes to a new island by boat. Jeff Probst teased the players with a merge, then dropped the real twist: a swap into three tribes. He said the swap was built for 18 players, but with Rob Antonson gone, the 17 left would form two tribes of six and one tribe of five. The players drew buffs from a bag, and one purple buff was left over, filling the smaller tribe at five.\n\nThe new Savu (purple) was Jenna Doore, Ori Jean-Charles, Devin Way, Alexis Levine, and Jelly. The new Toka (yellow) was Mike Pinsky, Carter, Brady, Thien An Nguyen, Kristin Flickinger, and Maggie Nestor. The new Dina (red) was Kilby, Sharonda Cox, Lewis, Eric Macksoud, Linnea Capobianco, and Cristian Chavez. Dina got a bare beach with only a pot, a machete, and flint to restart from.\n\nKristin was the only original Savu player on a Toka tribe with five former Toka, and she worked to make herself useful by pointing out food and medicine around camp. She tried to patch things with Carter, who did not trust her. At Dina, Kilby told the Savu majority how badly his old tribe had treated him, and Eric took to him right away. Sharonda and Linnea saw the bond forming and worried it would split their majority. At Savu, Ori, Devin, and Jelly renewed the Helicopter Alliance, and Devin spent the day nudging Jelly and Ori together. Alexis warned Jenna that Devin had floated her name, but Jenna brought that straight back to Devin and pushed to keep the former Toka group together. Alexis asked Jenna to hand over her shoes as collateral for a promise. Jenna refused.\n\nThe Reward and Immunity Challenge was a bucket toss into a spinning ball maze. Dina finished first and Toka second, so both tribes won safety, plus a coffee kit for Dina and a pitcher of iced coffee for Toka. Savu, already down a player, went to Tribal Council.\n\nBack at Savu, Jenna asked Devin and Jelly to put their old Toka sides aside and vote out a former Savu player, naming Alexis. Alexis tried to widen the gap between Jenna and Devin, but Devin, Jelly, and Ori held together. Jenna and Alexis voted for each other. The other three sent Jenna out 4 to 1 on Day 9, the fourth player voted out of the season.",
