   "recapStatus": "Drafted",
   "recap": "Episode 5, Not Here to Get a Pedicure, covered Days 9 and 10. Two tribes went to Tribal Council and two players left the game.\n\nSavu opened the episode with the four remaining players sharing the reasons they came out to play. Ori Jean-Charles talked about helping his single mother, Alexis Levine talked about her history with substance abuse, and Devin Way talked about the two brothers he lost.\n\nThe Reward and Immunity Challenge was do or die, with only the first tribe safe. Three players from each tribe dove for buoys and carried them over a balance beam, and a fourth threw them into three baskets. Mike Pinsky threw for Toka, Sharonda Cox for Dina, and Ori for Savu. Dina and Savu fell behind while gathering buoys, so Mike was the only thrower who got to work. Toka won the basket of pastries and the only safety in the game. Savu and Dina both went to Tribal Council.\n\nBack at camp, Toka found a note saying one of them was needed somewhere else. That player had to give up the reward and pick a tribe to visit. Mike, Maggie Nestor, and Kristin Flickinger volunteered, and Maggie was drawn. Her second note held the Alliance Builder Extra Vote, which had to be given to a player at the Tribal Council she attended. Maggie picked Dina, where her old Toka allies Danny Kilby and Lewis Kelly were outnumbered four to two. She gave them two extra votes, the new one plus one of her own.\n\nAt Savu, Devin pushed Alexis to join him and Jelly Loblack against Ori. Alexis went the other way and committed to Ori, then worked on Jelly to vote out Devin. Jelly weighed betraying the Helicopter Alliance against sending a fifth woman out of the game. Ori chose the alliance. Devin, Jelly, and Ori voted Alexis out 3 to 1, and Alexis voted Devin. She left in 16th place.\n\nAt Dina, Lewis tried a bluff before Maggie arrived. He told Sharonda that his Irish wedding ring was a blood ring that tied their games together and would turn into an idol for her later. Sharonda asked to see the paperwork, and Cristian Chavez recognized the ring from an earlier conversation with Lewis. The advantage was invented.\n\nMaggie's extra votes let Kilby and Lewis each write Linnea Capobianco's name twice. Kilby worried about a rock draw, and Lewis was ready. The first vote tied 4 to 4 between Lewis and Linnea, with Cristian, Eric Macksoud, Linnea, and Sharonda voting Lewis, and the two double ballots voting Linnea. The revote tied 4 to 4 again. With a deadlock, Eric, Kilby, Sharonda, and Cristian had to agree on one name or face rocks. Kilby refused to send Lewis home. The other three gave in, and Linnea left by unanimous decision, 15th out of the game. Nobody drew a rock.\n\nFourteen players remain.",
